                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "91606263-d482-3c71-aa88-8c2edb68156c",
                                        "entry_id": "d85c72fe-124e-337d-8199-709c20889ccc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A boundary or accepted division; a border."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8999a4bb-df78-404c-9199-24a3b48a6b00",
                                                "sense_id": "91606263-d482-3c71-aa88-8c2edb68156c",
                                                "text": "She lives on the borderline between reality and madness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c23ef819-95f6-4a79-ba16-1a707c252146",
                                                "sense_id": "91606263-d482-3c71-aa88-8c2edb68156c",
                                                "text": "Elbow deep inside the borderline\nShow me that you love me and that we belong together\nShoulder deep within the borderline\nRelax, turn around and take my hand"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "24cb1607-1a3d-3743-82f9-f141742ee6a9",
                                        "entry_id": "d85c72fe-124e-337d-8199-709c20889ccc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of borderline personality disorder."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7a20bef-fa48-4f10-a25f-4aee57832b38",
                                                "sense_id": "24cb1607-1a3d-3743-82f9-f141742ee6a9",
                                                "text": "The four overlapping concepts of borderline were as follows : (1) A residual model […] (2) An affective disorder model, which considered BPD as an affective spectrum illness displaying prominent[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f17f3bec-96a4-4aae-8477-360af7dd472b",
                                                "sense_id": "24cb1607-1a3d-3743-82f9-f141742ee6a9",
                                                "text": "[...] you should consider it! People with Borderline are especially affected by the unconditional affection parenting a pet can provide."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48a91679-c1ba-4382-bc3d-e879d90187ca",
                                                "sense_id": "24cb1607-1a3d-3743-82f9-f141742ee6a9",
                                                "text": "Subsequent conceptualizations of borderline were based on important contributions from psychoanalysts, […] As a result of its inclusion, appearing as “borderline personality disorder,” the construct gained legitimacy[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1701773e-3260-3d3f-ba1f-f1c7101deffe",
                                        "entry_id": "d85c72fe-124e-337d-8199-709c20889ccc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who has borderline personality disorder."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6e66989-7167-4566-8378-2192f829b09f",
                                                "sense_id": "1701773e-3260-3d3f-ba1f-f1c7101deffe",
                                                "text": "As an example of their affective profile, borderlines are set apart from passive aggressives by having more marked social anxiety […] and greater sensitivity […]"
                                            }
